  {'id':'d282_107','subject':'da-282','question':'Match horticulture branches: Col A: 1-Pomology, 2-Olericulture, 3-Floriculture, 4-Spices. Col B: P-condiments, Q-fruits, R-flowers, S-vegetables. Col C: i-rose, ii-mango, iii-tomato, iv-cardamom','options':['1-Q-ii, 2-S-iii, 3-R-i, 4-P-iv','1-P-iv, 2-Q-ii, 3-S-iii, 4-R-i','1-R-i, 2-P-iv, 3-Q-ii, 4-S-iii','1-S-iii, 2-R-i, 3-P-iv, 4-Q-ii'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Pomology (fruits=mango=ii), Olericulture (vegetables=tomato=iii), Floriculture (flowers=rose=i), Spices (condiments=cardamom=iv).','difficulty':'hard'},
  {'id':'d282_108','subject':'da-282','question':'The botanical name of tomato is:','options':['Solanum melongena','Solanum lycopersicum','Abelmoschus esculentus','Capsicum annuum'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Tomato (Solanum lycopersicum) belongs to family Solanaceae. It is the most widely grown vegetable globally.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_109','subject':'da-282','question':'Bhendi (Okra/Ladyfinger) belongs to which plant family?','options':['Solanaceae','Cucurbitaceae','Malvaceae','Leguminosae'],'correct':2,'explanation':'Bhendi/Okra (Abelmoschus esculentus) belongs to family Malvaceae (Hibiscus family). It is rich in fiber and vitamins.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_110','subject':'da-282','question':'The botanical name of rose is:','options':['Chrysanthemum morifolium','Rosa indica','Tagetes erecta','Jasminum sambac'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Rose (Rosa indica/Rosa hybrida) belongs to family Rosaceae and is the most important commercial flower crop.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_111','subject':'da-282','question':'Marigold is botanically known as:','options':['Rosa indica','Chrysanthemum morifolium','Tagetes erecta','Jasminum sambac'],'correct':2,'explanation':'Marigold (Tagetes erecta) belongs to family Asteraceae. It is the most widely grown flower in India for festivals and garlands.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_112','subject':'da-282','question':'ASSERTION-REASON: Assertion (A): Post-harvest losses in horticultural crops are high (20-40%). Reason (R): Fruits, vegetables, and flowers are perishable with high moisture content, prone to mechanical damage and microbial spoilage.','options':['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A','A is true but R is false','A is false but R is true'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Post-harvest losses in horticulture are 20-40%. R correctly explains the cause — perishable nature and susceptibility to spoilage.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_113','subject':'da-282','question':'Black pepper (Piper nigrum) is called:','options':['King of Spices','Queen of Spices','Black Gold','Prince of Spices'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Black pepper is called the King of Spices and also Black Gold. It is the most widely traded spice in the world.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_114','subject':'da-282','question':'Cardamom is called the:','options':['King of Spices','Queen of Spices','King of Fruits','Spice King'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Cardamom (Elettaria cardamomum) is called the Queen of Spices. It is the third most expensive spice in the world.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_115','subject':'da-282','question':'Match vegetables: Col A: 1-Tomato, 2-Onion, 3-Bhendi, 4-Cabbage. Col B: P-Brassicaceae, Q-Solanaceae, R-Malvaceae, S-Liliaceae. Col C: i-leaves, ii-bulb, iii-fruit, iv-capsule fruit','options':['1-Q-iii, 2-S-ii, 3-R-iv, 4-P-i','1-P-i, 2-Q-iii, 3-S-ii, 4-R-iv','1-R-iv, 2-P-i, 3-Q-iii, 4-S-ii','1-S-ii, 2-R-iv, 3-P-i, 4-Q-iii'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Tomato (Solanaceae=fruit=iii), Onion (Liliaceae=bulb=ii), Bhendi (Malvaceae=capsule fruit=iv), Cabbage (Brassicaceae=leaves=i).','difficulty':'hard'},
  {'id':'d282_116','subject':'da-282','question':'The edible part of cauliflower is the:','options':['Root','Stem','Curd (compact flower head)','Leaf'],'correct':2,'explanation':'The edible part of cauliflower (Brassica oleracea var. botrytis) is the curd — a compact, immature flower head.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_117','subject':'da-282','question':'Guava (Psidium guajava) is considered a nutritious fruit because it is high in:','options':['Vitamin A','Vitamin C (highest among common fruits)','Calcium','Fat'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Guava has the highest Vitamin C content among common fruits — about 4-5 times more than oranges.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_118','subject':'da-282','question':'The botanical name of brinjal (eggplant) is:','options':['Solanum lycopersicum','Solanum melongena','Abelmoschus esculentus','Cucumis sativus'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Brinjal/Eggplant (Solanum melongena) belongs to family Solanaceae along with tomato, potato, and chilli.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_119','subject':'da-282','question':'ASSERTION-REASON: Assertion (A): Onion is a modified underground stem. Reason (R): Onion consists of fleshy scale leaves surrounding a central bud, all attached to a flattened compressed disc (stem).','options':['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A','A is true but R is false','A is false but R is true'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Onion is a tunicated bulb — a modified stem with fleshy scale leaves on a compressed disc. R correctly explains this botanical structure.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_120','subject':'da-282','question':'Match spices: Col A: 1-Cardamom, 2-Black pepper, 3-Turmeric, 4-Ginger. Col B: P-Zingiber officinale, Q-Curcuma longa, R-Piper nigrum, S-Elettaria cardamomum. Col C: i-Piperaceae, ii-Zingiberaceae family member, iii-Zingiberaceae, iv-Zingiberaceae','options':['1-S-iv, 2-R-i, 3-Q-iii, 4-P-ii','1-R-i, 2-S-iv, 3-P-ii, 4-Q-iii','1-P-ii, 2-Q-iii, 3-R-i, 4-S-iv','1-Q-iii, 2-P-ii, 3-S-iv, 4-R-i'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Cardamom (Elettaria=Zingiberaceae=iv), Black pepper (Piper=Piperaceae=i), Turmeric (Curcuma=Zingiberaceae=iii), Ginger (Zingiber=Zingiberaceae=ii).','difficulty':'hard'},
  {'id':'d282_121','subject':'da-282','question':'Floriculture deals with:','options':['Fruit production','Vegetable production','Flower and ornamental plant production','Spice production'],'correct':2,'explanation':'Floriculture deals with the cultivation of flowers and ornamental plants for decorative purposes, bouquets, and landscaping.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_122','subject':'da-282','question':'Grapes (Vitis vinifera) belong to which family?','options':['Anacardiaceae','Musaceae','Vitaceae','Rutaceae'],'correct':2,'explanation':'Grapes (Vitis vinifera) belong to family Vitaceae. Grapes are used for fresh consumption, wine, raisins, and juice.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_123','subject':'da-282','question':'Tomato is called the poor man\'s apple because:','options':['It is inexpensive and low in nutrition','It is high in Vitamin C, lycopene, and widely available at affordable prices','It resembles an apple in shape','It is grown only by poor farmers'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Tomato is called the poor man\'s apple due to high Vitamin C, lycopene (antioxidant), and wide availability at affordable prices.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_124','subject':'da-282','question':'ASSERTION-REASON: Assertion (A): Banana is a climacteric fruit. Reason (R): Climacteric fruits show a rise in respiration rate and ethylene production during ripening, and can ripen after harvest.','options':['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A','A is true but R is false','A is false but R is true'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Banana is climacteric — it ripens after harvest with a rise in ethylene. R correctly defines climacteric behavior.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_125','subject':'da-282','question':'Coconut is botanically classified as a:','options':['True fruit','Berry','Drupe (stone fruit)','Nut'],'correct':2,'explanation':'Coconut (Cocos nucifera) is a drupe (stone fruit) with a fibrous outer husk (exocarp), hard shell (endocarp), and edible flesh (endosperm).','difficulty':'hard'},
  {'id':'d282_126','subject':'da-282','question':'Which is a plantation crop in horticulture?','options':['Tomato','Paddy','Coconut','Marigold'],'correct':2,'explanation':'Plantation crops are perennial crops grown on large estates. Coconut is a plantation crop along with tea, coffee, rubber, and cashew.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_127','subject':'da-282','question':'Turmeric (Curcuma longa) is propagated commercially by:','options':['Seeds','Rhizomes','Stem cuttings','Grafting'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Turmeric is propagated vegetatively through rhizomes (underground stems). Seeds are not used for commercial production.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_128','subject':'da-282','question':'ASSERTION-REASON: Assertion (A): Drip irrigation is highly suitable for horticultural crops. Reason (R): Drip irrigation delivers water directly to the root zone, reducing water loss and improving water use efficiency.','options':['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A','A is true but R is false','A is false but R is true'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Drip irrigation is ideal for horticulture because it precisely delivers water to roots, reducing evaporation and weed growth. R correctly explains A.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_129','subject':'da-282','question':'Jasmine (Mogra) used in garlands belongs to which family?','options':['Rosaceae','Asteraceae','Oleaceae','Malvaceae'],'correct':2,'explanation':'Jasmine (Jasminum sambac) belongs to family Oleaceae (Olive family). It is India\'s most important cut flower and garland flower.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_130','subject':'da-282','question':'Match fruit types: Col A: 1-Mango, 2-Banana, 3-Grape, 4-Guava. Col B: P-Vitaceae, Q-Myrtaceae, R-Anacardiaceae, S-Musaceae. Col C: i-Mangifera indica, ii-Psidium guajava, iii-Vitis vinifera, iv-Musa paradisiaca','options':['1-R-i, 2-S-iv, 3-P-iii, 4-Q-ii','1-P-iii, 2-Q-ii, 3-R-i, 4-S-iv','1-S-iv, 2-R-i, 3-Q-ii, 4-P-iii','1-Q-ii, 2-P-iii, 3-S-iv, 4-R-i'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Mango (Anacardiaceae=Mangifera indica=i), Banana (Musaceae=Musa=iv), Grape (Vitaceae=Vitis vinifera=iii), Guava (Myrtaceae=Psidium=ii).','difficulty':'hard'},
  {'id':'d282_131','subject':'da-282','question':'The edible part of potato (Solanum tuberosum) is a:','options':['Root','Fruit','Tuber (modified underground stem)','Bulb'],'correct':2,'explanation':'Potato\'s edible part is a tuber — a swollen underground stem with stored starch and eyes (buds) for vegetative propagation.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_132','subject':'da-282','question':'Citrus fruits belong to which botanical family?','options':['Anacardiaceae','Rosaceae','Rutaceae','Vitaceae'],'correct':2,'explanation':'Citrus fruits (orange, lemon, lime, grapefruit) belong to family Rutaceae. The genus Citrus includes most common citrus fruits.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_133','subject':'da-282','question':'The edible part of carrot is a:','options':['Bulb','Tuber','Taproot','Corm'],'correct':2,'explanation':'The edible part of carrot (Daucus carota) is a modified taproot that stores carbohydrates and beta-carotene (Vitamin A precursor).','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_134','subject':'da-282','question':'ASSERTION-REASON: Assertion (A): Chilli is both a vegetable and a spice. Reason (R): Green chilli is used as a vegetable while dry red chilli is used as a spice; both come from Capsicum annuum.','options':['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A','A is true but R is false','A is false but R is true'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Chilli is dual-purpose — green fruit as vegetable, dry red as spice. R correctly explains both uses come from Capsicum annuum.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_135','subject':'da-282','question':'Cucumber (Cucumis sativus) belongs to family:','options':['Solanaceae','Cucurbitaceae','Malvaceae','Brassicaceae'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Cucumber belongs to family Cucurbitaceae (gourd family), along with bottle gourd, pumpkin, bitter gourd, and watermelon.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_136','subject':'da-282','question':'Pomegranate (Punica granatum) is used medicinally because it is rich in:','options':['Vitamin D','Antioxidants including punicalagins and anthocyanins','Calcium only','Carbohydrates'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Pomegranate is rich in antioxidants (punicalagins, punicic acid, anthocyanins) and Vitamin C, used for heart health and immunity.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_137','subject':'da-282','question':'Match flowers: Col A: 1-Rose, 2-Jasmine, 3-Marigold, 4-Chrysanthemum. Col B: P-Asteraceae, Q-Rosaceae, R-Oleaceae, S-Asteraceae. Col C: i-temple offerings, ii-garland and cut flower, iii-perfume and garland, iv-cut flower','options':['1-Q-ii, 2-R-iii, 3-P-i, 4-S-iv','1-P-i, 2-Q-ii, 3-R-iii, 4-S-iv','1-R-iii, 2-P-i, 3-S-iv, 4-Q-ii','1-S-iv, 2-P-i, 3-Q-ii, 4-R-iii'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Rose (Rosaceae=garland/cut=ii), Jasmine (Oleaceae=perfume/garland=iii), Marigold (Asteraceae=temple=i), Chrysanthemum (Asteraceae=cut flower=iv).','difficulty':'hard'},
  {'id':'d282_138','subject':'da-282','question':'Which queen of spice is the third most expensive spice in the world?','options':['Black pepper','Turmeric','Cardamom','Ginger'],'correct':2,'explanation':'Cardamom (Elettaria cardamomum), called Queen of Spices, is the third most expensive spice after saffron and vanilla.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_139','subject':'da-282','question':'ASSERTION-REASON: Assertion (A): Bitter gourd is used to control blood sugar. Reason (R): Bitter gourd (Momordica charantia) contains insulin-like compounds (charantin, polypeptide-p) that lower blood glucose.','options':['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A','A is true but R is false','A is false but R is true'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Bitter gourd is used in Ayurveda for diabetes management. R correctly explains the biochemical basis — charantin and polypeptide-p.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_140','subject':'da-282','question':'Which fruit is known as the Queen of Fruits?','options':['Mango','Banana','Mangosteen','Papaya'],'correct':2,'explanation':'Mangosteen (Garcinia mangostana) is called the Queen of Fruits due to its exquisite taste and nutritional value.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_141','subject':'da-282','question':'The active antioxidant compound lycopene is found mainly in:','options':['Mango','Tomato (especially cooked/processed)','Banana','Cabbage'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Lycopene is a powerful antioxidant carotenoid found abundantly in tomatoes, especially in processed forms like tomato paste and ketchup.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_142','subject':'da-282','question':'Ginger (Zingiber officinale) is propagated by:','options':['Seeds','Rhizomes','Stem cuttings','Layering'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Ginger is propagated vegetatively through rhizomes (underground stems). The rhizome pieces with nodes are planted for commercial cultivation.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_143','subject':'da-282','question':'ASSERTION-REASON: Assertion (A): Tissue culture is used in horticulture for rapid propagation of plants. Reason (R): Tissue culture produces large numbers of disease-free, genetically uniform plants quickly from a small tissue sample.','options':['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A','A is true but R is false','A is false but R is true'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Tissue culture (micropropagation) is widely used for banana, orchid, and potato propagation. R correctly explains the advantages.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_144','subject':'da-282','question':'Which vegetable is botanically a fruit (has seeds inside)?','options':['Potato','Carrot','Tomato','Cabbage'],'correct':2,'explanation':'Botanically, tomato is a fruit because it develops from the flower\'s ovary and contains seeds. Culinary use treats it as a vegetable.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_145','subject':'da-282','question':'The major coconut producing states in India include:','options':['Punjab, Haryana, UP','Kerala, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu, Andhra Pradesh','Bihar, West Bengal, Assam','Rajasthan, Gujarat, Maharashtra'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Kerala, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu, and Andhra Pradesh are the major coconut producing states, with Kerala being the largest producer.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_146','subject':'da-282','question':'Match edible parts of vegetables: Col A: 1-Carrot, 2-Potato, 3-Onion, 4-Cauliflower. Col B: P-bulb, Q-curd, R-taproot, S-tuber. Col C: i-modified stem, ii-modified stem-leaves, iii-modified root, iv-flower head','options':['1-R-iii, 2-S-i, 3-P-ii, 4-Q-iv','1-P-ii, 2-Q-iv, 3-R-iii, 4-S-i','1-S-i, 2-P-ii, 3-Q-iv, 4-R-iii','1-Q-iv, 2-R-iii, 3-S-i, 4-P-ii'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Carrot (taproot=modified root=iii), Potato (tuber=modified stem=i), Onion (bulb=modified stem-leaves=ii), Cauliflower (curd=flower head=iv).','difficulty':'hard'},
  {'id':'d282_147','subject':'da-282','question':'Which is a non-climacteric fruit that does NOT ripen further after harvest?','options':['Mango','Banana','Papaya','Grape'],'correct':3,'explanation':'Grape is non-climacteric — it does not continue to ripen after harvest. Non-climacteric fruits must be harvested at full ripeness.','difficulty':'hard'},
  {'id':'d282_148','subject':'da-282','question':'The botanical name of papaya is:','options':['Mangifera indica','Carica papaya','Musa paradisiaca','Punica granatum'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Papaya (Carica papaya) belongs to family Caricaceae. It is a tropical fruit rich in Vitamin C, Vitamin A, and the enzyme papain.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_149','subject':'da-282','question':'ASSERTION-REASON: Assertion (A): Rose is the most important commercial flower crop in India. Reason (R): Rose has the highest demand for cut flowers, loose flowers, rose water, and essential oil, making it commercially most valuable.','options':['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A','A is true but R is false','A is false but R is true'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Rose is the leading commercial flower globally and in India. R correctly explains the diverse uses that make it commercially most valuable.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_150','subject':'da-282','question':'Match plantation crops: Col A: 1-Coconut, 2-Coffee, 3-Tea, 4-Rubber. Col B: P-Euphorbiaceae, Q-Arecaceae, R-Rubiaceae, S-Theaceae. Col C: i-Hevea brasiliensis, ii-Cocos nucifera, iii-Coffea arabica, iv-Camellia sinensis','options':['1-Q-ii, 2-R-iii, 3-S-iv, 4-P-i','1-P-i, 2-Q-ii, 3-R-iii, 4-S-iv','1-S-iv, 2-P-i, 3-Q-ii, 4-R-iii','1-R-iii, 2-S-iv, 3-P-i, 4-Q-ii'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Coconut (Arecaceae=Cocos nucifera=ii), Coffee (Rubiaceae=Coffea arabica=iii), Tea (Theaceae=Camellia sinensis=iv), Rubber (Euphorbiaceae=Hevea brasiliensis=i).','difficulty':'hard'},
  {'id':'d282_151','subject':'da-282','question':'The enzyme papain found in papaya is commercially used for:','options':['Making wine','Meat tenderizing and pharmaceutical industry','Paper production','Pesticide making'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Papain is a proteolytic (protein-digesting) enzyme from papaya used in meat tenderizers, pharmaceutical preparations, and textile industry.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_152','subject':'da-282','question':'Which part of the onion plant is used as a spice?','options':['Stem','Bulb (modified underground stem)','Leaf','Root'],'correct':1,'explanation':'The bulb of onion is used as both a vegetable and spice. It is a tunicated bulb with fleshy scale leaves on a compressed stem disc.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_153','subject':'da-282','question':'ASSERTION-REASON: Assertion (A): Cold storage is essential for extending shelf life of horticultural produce. Reason (R): Low temperatures slow down respiration, enzymatic activity, and microbial growth in perishable horticultural crops.','options':['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A','A is true but R is false','A is false but R is true'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Cold storage extends shelf life. R correctly explains the mechanism — low temperatures slow respiration and microbial spoilage.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_154','subject':'da-282','question':'Which compound in turmeric has anti-inflammatory and antioxidant properties?','options':['Piperine','Curcumin','Capsaicin','Allicin'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Curcumin is the main active compound in turmeric (Curcuma longa) responsible for its yellow color, anti-inflammatory, and antioxidant properties.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_155','subject':'da-282','question':'Cashew nut (Anacardium occidentale) belongs to which family?','options':['Rutaceae','Myrtaceae','Anacardiaceae','Vitaceae'],'correct':2,'explanation':'Cashew (Anacardium occidentale) belongs to family Anacardiaceae, same family as mango. Goa, Kerala, and Andhra Pradesh are major producers.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_156','subject':'da-282','question':'Which of the following is a cruciferous vegetable (family Brassicaceae)?','options':['Tomato','Bhendi','Cabbage','Brinjal'],'correct':2,'explanation':'Cabbage (Brassica oleracea var. capitata) belongs to family Brassicaceae (Cruciferae). Other cruciferous vegetables include cauliflower, broccoli, and radish.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_157','subject':'da-282','question':'ASSERTION-REASON: Assertion (A): Grafting is commonly used for propagating mango. Reason (R): Grafting ensures that the new plant has the same desirable characteristics as the parent plant and comes to bearing earlier than seedlings.','options':['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A','A is true but R is false','A is false but R is true'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Mango is propagated by grafting (veneer/inarching) for true-to-type plants that bear fruit earlier. R correctly explains the advantages of grafting.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_158','subject':'da-282','question':'The water requirement of drip irrigation compared to flood irrigation is:','options':['More water (2x more)','Same amount of water','Less water (saves 30-50%)','Depends on crop only'],'correct':2,'explanation':'Drip irrigation saves 30-50% water compared to flood irrigation by delivering water directly to roots, reducing evaporation and runoff.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_159','subject':'da-282','question':'Which state is the largest producer of mango in India?','options':['Tamil Nadu','Karnataka','Maharashtra','Uttar Pradesh'],'correct':3,'explanation':'Uttar Pradesh is the largest producer of mango in India, followed by Andhra Pradesh and Telangana. Dasheri and Langra are famous UP varieties.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d282_160','subject':'da-282','question':'Match: Col A: 1-Mango variety, 2-Banana variety, 3-Grape variety, 4-Citrus type. Col B: P-Robusta, Q-Bangalore Blue, R-Alphonso, S-Nagpur Orange. Col C: i-Maharashtra specialty, ii-Robusta tissue culture variety, iii-Hapus/prized mango, iv-wine grape from Karnataka','options':['1-R-iii, 2-P-ii, 3-Q-iv, 4-S-i','1-P-ii, 2-Q-iv, 3-R-iii, 4-S-i','1-S-i, 2-R-iii, 3-P-ii, 4-Q-iv','1-Q-iv, 2-S-i, 3-P-ii, 4-R-iii'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Mango (Alphonso/Hapus=prized=iii), Banana (Robusta=tissue culture variety=ii), Grape (Bangalore Blue=wine grape Karnataka=iv), Citrus (Nagpur Orange=Maharashtra=i).','difficulty':'hard'},
  {'id':'d282_161','subject':'da-282','question':'The compound capsaicin that gives chilli its pungency belongs to which chemical class?','options':['Alkaloid','Terpene','Flavonoid','Carotenoid'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Capsaicin is a vanilloid alkaloid responsible for the pungent heat of chilli (Capsicum). It binds to pain receptors (TRPV1) in the mouth.','difficulty':'hard'},
  {'id':'d282_162','subject':'da-282','question':'ASSERTION-REASON: Assertion (A): Vegetables are broadly classified based on edible parts. Reason (R): Different parts of vegetables (roots, stems, leaves, flowers, fruits, seeds) are consumed, and crops are classified accordingly.','options':['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A','A is true but R is false','A is false but R is true'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Vegetables are classified by edible part — root vegetables (carrot), stem (potato), leaf (cabbage), flower (cauliflower), fruit (tomato), seed (pea). R explains A.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d282_163','subject':'da-282','question':'Onion cultivation in India is most prominent in which state?','options':['Punjab','Maharashtra','Uttar Pradesh','Rajasthan'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Maharashtra (especially Nashik) is the largest onion producing state in India, contributing about 35% of national production.','difficulty':'medium'},
